<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Osraige</h1><p class="st-meta">400 CE – 1541 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Irish kingdom between Leinster and Munster, centred on Kilkenny, whose Mac Giolla Phádraig rulers survived as lords until the Tudor surrender of 1541.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Osraige emerged in early medieval Ireland as the kingdom of a people living in the valleys of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-nore">Nore</a> and its tributaries, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-kilkenny">County Kilkenny</a> and south <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-loigis">Laois</a>. Its kings traced descent from ancestors distinct from both the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Laigin</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganachta</a>, and the kingdom stood between the Kingdom of Leinster and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Kingdom of Munster</a>, usually as a tributary of Munster.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The monasteries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seir-kieran">Saighir</a>, linked with St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciaran-of-saighir">Ciarán</a>, and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghaboe">Aghaboe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a>, where St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canice">Canice</a> is honoured, were centres of learning and gave their names to the diocese of Ossory. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerball-mac-dunlainge">Cerball mac Dúnlainge</a>, who died in 888, made Osraige a major power by fighting and allying with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> leaders. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-giolla-phadraig">Mac Giolla Phádraig</a>, briefly held the kingship of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donnchad-mac-gilla-patraic">Donnchad mac Gilla Pátraic</a> in the 1030s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-norman-invasion-of-ireland">Anglo-Norman invasion</a> of 1169, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> became the seat of English lords, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-giolla-phadraig">Mac Giolla Phádraig</a> held only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-ossory">Upper Ossory</a>. In 1541 their chief, Brian, surrendered his lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> and received them back as Baron of Upper Ossory, ending the kingdom.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-osraige.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Osraige" width="320" height="418"><figcaption>Image: Erigena · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Osraige-900.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 CE – 1541 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cerball mac Dúnlainge, Donnchad mac Gilla Pátraic, Brian Mac Giolla Phádraig</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish, later Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Osraige, Ossory</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=970&amp;focus=kingdom-of-osraige" aria-label="Kingdom of Osraige on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4518 362 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Osraige lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4838 618L4823 622M4838 618L4861 599M4838 618L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4823 622h0M4861 599h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4838 618h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4838 618h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=970&amp;focus=kingdom-of-osraige">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
